# Copy to .env and fill in from your Supabase project's settings
# (Dashboard → Project Settings → API / API Keys).
#
# Prefer to develop against a throwaway database on your own machine? You do
# not need to fill anything in here:
#
#   npm run db:start    # boots the local stack (needs Docker)
#   npm run db:env      # writes .env.local pointing at it
#
# Vite loads .env.local after .env, so it wins while it exists; delete it to
# point back at whatever is configured here. See README → "Local development
# database".

# Required — safe to expose to the browser.
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# Optional — only needed for `npm run db:types` when PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is a
# custom domain (the script normally derives the ref from the URL, and uses
# the local stack automatically when the URL points at 127.0.0.1).
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=

# Optional — server-only, bypasses Row Level Security.
# Only needed if you use createSupabaseAdminClient() (src/lib/supabase.server.ts)
# or DEV_AUTO_LOGIN below. NEVER prefix with PUBLIC_, never commit a real value.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional — transactional email via Resend (see src/lib/server/email.ts).
# Server-only, never prefix with PUBLIC_. Without RESEND_API_KEY, sendEmail()
# logs each message to the console instead of sending and reports failure.
# EMAIL_FROM must be a sender on a domain verified in your Resend dashboard
# ("Acme <onboarding@resend.dev>" works for trying it out).
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# EMAIL_FROM=Acme <onboarding@resend.dev>
# EMAIL_REPLY_TO=support@example.com

# Optional — geocoding (see src/lib/server/geocode.ts). Server-only. When an
# address is saved on a record page, GEOCODER_URL is fetched with the address
# in place of {query} (and GEOCODER_API_KEY in place of {key}) and the first
# Nominatim-style match's lat/lon is stored with the address — which is what
# puts a record on a view's map. Without it addresses save with no coordinates.
# Public Nominatim asks for a user agent that names your app and allows one
# request per second; a hosted provider (LocationIQ, Geoapify) wants a key.
# GEOCODER_URL=https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search?format=json&limit=1&q={query}
# GEOCODER_URL=https://us1.locationiq.com/v1/search?key={key}&format=json&limit=1&q={query}
# GEOCODER_API_KEY=
# GEOCODER_USER_AGENT=my-app/1.0 (ops@example.com)

# Optional — the map on a view page (see src/lib/map.ts and
# src/lib/components/map-view/). A MapLibre style URL; its origin is added to
# the Content-Security-Policy, and the style's tiles, glyphs and sprite must
# come from that origin too (true of the free demo style and of OpenFreeMap).
# The dark URL is used when the reader's theme is dark; leave it unset to use
# one style for both. Without a URL the map layout says it is not configured.
# PUBLIC_MAP_STYLE_URL=https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty
# PUBLIC_MAP_STYLE_URL_DARK=https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/dark

# Optional — development auto-login (see src/lib/server/dev-auto-login.ts).
# Signs every request in as DEV_AUTO_LOGIN_EMAIL so `npm run dev` lands you
# straight in the app. Requires SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY. This is an auth
# bypass: never set it in a deployed production environment (it also refuses
# to run when VERCEL_ENV=production).
# DEV_AUTO_LOGIN=true
# DEV_AUTO_LOGIN_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Optional — credentials the Playwright suite signs in with. Default to the
# users in supabase/seed.sql, so the local stack needs no configuration here.
# E2E_USER_EMAIL=dev@example.com
# E2E_USER_PASSWORD=password123

# Optional — the AI assistant (see src/lib/server/ai/ and docs/assistant.md).
# Server-only, never prefix with PUBLIC_. Without ANTHROPIC_API_KEY the
# /assistant page renders but says it is not configured, and the stream
# endpoint answers 503. AI_MODEL overrides the model id (default claude-opus-5).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# AI_MODEL=claude-opus-5
